<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007) & Morelli et al. (2009) zebrafish Delta-Notch delayed Kuramoto phase synchrony on an advected FGF8/Wnt-graded PSM lattice: kinematic waves, Mib1-gated coupling, emergent DAPT ALD/PRP (Danio rerio (zebrafish presomitic mesoderm & paraxial somites); vendored SEM specimen is a chick (Gallus gallus) embryo used as a vertebrate somite-metamere stand-in)" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-6> ;
    schema:about "Danio rerio (zebrafish presomitic mesoderm & paraxial somites); vendored SEM specimen is a chick (Gallus gallus) embryo used as a vertebrate somite-metamere stand-in" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: PSM shortening and the Soroldoni (2014) Doppler contribution to the segmentation period, cell division/ingression in the tailbud, 3D cell sorting, explicit Mib1 E3-ligase stoichiometry or measured Delta endocytosis rates, or a boundary profile derived from the phase pattern (chi(s) is a coherence-gated synthetic rendering)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Advected 24 x 12 AP x lateral nearest-neighbour delayed Kuramoto PSM lattice (open AP, periodic lateral, per-column period-scaled delay) under a tailbud-anchored exponential FGF8/Wnt frequency profile (f_A = 0.5): N_w = 1.58 kinematic waves (analytic 1.61), anterior wavelength 2.21 S (analytic 2.00 S), N_w monotone in f_A (2.52 -> -0.03 for f_A 0.3 -> 1.0)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Bilateral dorsal somite row DoG peak segmentation on the vendored SEM (48.47 px mean spacing, symmetry ratio 0.9606, fitted-sinusoid r = 0.563)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Emergent ALD/PRP from R_crit = 0.5 crossings of the half-period-smoothed front lateral order parameter + Delta_n_det = 2.5: 5-seed means ALD = 5.41 / 9.21 / 14.24 (obs 5.4 / 9.6 / 14.4), PRP = 14.86 (obs 14.7), RMSE 0.22 somites, Pearson r = 0.9998 (0.9986 over the 4 perturbed regimes); somite stage clock-counted at Omega(kappa(t)) so continuous DAPT lengthens the period from 22.18 to 25.00 min",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Mib1-gated coupling kappa(t) = kappa_max u(t) g(t) with ubiquitination ODE (k_ub = 0.08, k_endo = 0.02 min^-1, u_ss^WT = 0.8) and gamma-secretase gate with 8-min DAPT clearance; mib1-null late R = 0.28 (ALD 5.8), Mib1 restoration at s = 9 rescues to R = 0.77 (PRP 15.3); dose sweep monotone",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Transcendental collective frequency solver and 2D (tau_c, kappa) linear stability tongue (T_sync = 22.18 min, kappa_eff = 0.0623 min^-1 at tau_c = 20.5 min vs -0.0353 min^-1 at tau_c = 11.0 min)",
        "reported_in_source: Itoh et al. (2003): Mind bomb E3 ubiquitin ligase ubiquitinates Delta, required for Delta endocytosis and trans-activation of Notch; mib^ta52b abolishes Delta-Notch signalling",
        "reported_in_source: Morelli et al. (2009) frequency profile omega(x) and kinematic phase waves k = (Omega - omega(x))/v travelling posterior -> anterior; Soroldoni et al. (2014) order 1-2 waves across the zebrafish PSM, waves slowing anteriorly; Herrgen et al. (2010) DAPT lengthens the segmentation period",
        "reported_in_source: Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007) Science 317:1911-1915 & Morelli et al. (2009) HFSP J. 3:55-66 delayed Kuramoto phase-oscillator model dtheta_i/dt = omega_i + (kappa/z)*sum_j sin(theta_j(t - tau_c) - theta_i(t)) + xi_i(t), collective frequency shift Omega = omega_0 - kappa*sin(Omega*tau_c), linear stability stiffness kappa_eff = kappa*cos(Omega*tau_c) > 0",
        "reported_in_source: Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007): DAPT pulse-chase Anterior Limit of Defects ALD(s_in) = s_in + ~5.5 somites (obs 5.4 +/- 0.8, 9.6 +/- 0.9, 14.4 +/- 0.9 for s_in = 0, 4, 9) and Posterior Rescue Point PRP = 14.7 +/- 1.1 after washout at s_out = 9; mib/aei/des/bea mutants desynchronise like early DAPT",
        "transfer_boundary: The SEM specimen is a chick embryo (Wikimedia 'Aves Neural tube and somites in chick embryo'), used as a vertebrate somite-metamere stand-in; no zebrafish her1/deltaC in-situ wave pattern is vendored",
        "transfer_boundary: The frequency profile is a single exponential with f_A = 0.5 and L = 6 S chosen to land in the 1-2-wave range reported for zebrafish; it is not digitised from Morelli (2009) Fig. 3 or Soroldoni (2014) kymographs, and the N_w measurement's reference value is the model's own analytic law",
        "transfer_boundary: k_ub, k_endo, tau_wash, DAPT dose/IC50 and Hill n are the script's reduced rate constants; D_phi = 0.003 rad^2/min, sigma_omega = 0.014 rad/min and tau_wash = 8 min were calibrated so the emergent ALD/PRP lags match the Riedel-Kruse (2007) data (as the paper fitted its desynchronisation rate)",
        "transfer_boundary: tau_c(x) omega(x) = const (coupling delay scales with the local period) is this script's assumption; the Eulerian-delay alternative was not simulated" ;
