<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007) & Morelli et al. (2009) zebrafish Delta-Notch delayed Kuramoto phase synchrony on an advected FGF8/Wnt-graded PSM lattice: kinematic waves, Mib1-gated coupling, emergent DAPT ALD/PRP — Code-to-model traceability: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Laws 1-6 are stated in the docstring with their Lean theorem names (L68-118), every modelling function's docstring names its law and source (L218-226, L291-298, L327-331, L387-407), the loop body is annotated per mechanism (L486, L495, L501, L517, L523), and `math_kg_loops/riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.yaml` maps each of the 6 laws to Lean loci and code loci (YAML L13-224). Deductions: the exponential profile, the delay scaling and the Mib1/DAPT rate constants are traced to a declared-assumption paragraph (L55-66) rather than to any equation or figure of a source (-5); the 0.05 rad tailbud seeding noise (L527), the half-period smoothing window (L454) and the chi(s) rendering constants (L598-604) are uncited (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py L527–L527: Tailbud seeding noise 0.05 rad is an uncited constant <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py#L527-L527>",
        "2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py L55–L66: Reduced assumptions (profile form, delay scaling, rate constants, calibration) declared but not traceable to source equations <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py#L55-L66>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007) & Morelli et al. (2009) zebrafish Delta-Notch delayed Kuramoto phase synchrony on an advected FGF8/Wnt-graded PSM lattice: kinematic waves, Mib1-gated coupling, emergent DAPT ALD/PRP — Model fidelity to source: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The lattice equation is now exactly the source model: nearest-neighbour delayed coupling (kappa/z_i) sum_j sin(theta_j(t - tau_c,j) - theta_i) with open AP / periodic lateral boundaries (L501-515), the ad hoc 1.6 kappa_eff sin(psi - theta) term and the 0.35/0.65 blend of Pass 2 are gone, the collective frequency / stiffness solver is unchanged (L213-266) and the kinematic steady state used for initialisation is the Law-4 solution k = (Omega/v)(1 - c) (L432-437); the emergent segmentation period of the lattice (22.18 min WT, 25.00 min DAPT) matches the solver. Deductions: the frequency profile is a single exponential with f_A = 0.5 (L284-319), not Morelli's profile (-3); the per-column delay scaling tau_c(x) omega(x) = const (L413) is a modelling choice introduced to keep the anterior coupling attractive, and Panel B only marks the unscaled point rather than simulating it (-3); Mib1 kinetics are a two-rate linear ODE with unmeasured k_ub, k_endo (L172-173, L495-499) and the DAPT gate is a Hill function with assumed dose/IC50 = 20 and n = 2 (L174-176) (-2); advection is a discrete one-column shift with tailbud seeding from the last column plus 0.05 rad noise (L523-531), with no cell division or PSM shortening (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py L171–L176: k_ub, k_endo, tau_wash, dose ratio and Hill n are declared reduced constants without measured sources <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py#L171-L176>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-model-fidelity-5> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007) & Morelli et al. (2009) zebrafish Delta-Notch delayed Kuramoto phase synchrony on an advected FGF8/Wnt-graded PSM lattice: kinematic waves, Mib1-gated coupling, emergent DAPT ALD/PRP — Morphometric validation: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The validation is now genuine where Pass 2's was circular: emergent ALD/PRP from the simulated coherence trajectory are compared with the Riedel-Kruse (2007) observations across 5 regimes and 5 seeds (ALD 5.41 / 9.21 / 14.24 vs 5.4 / 9.6 / 14.4 somites, PRP 14.86 vs 14.7; RMSE 0.22 somites, all within 1 observed SD; `evaluate_dapt_regimes` L661-715, `regime_validation_statistics` L718-744) and 8 measurements carry references and units (L863-964). Deductions: D_phi, sigma_omega and tau_wash were calibrated against these same ALD/PRP data (L161-162, L174), so only the unit slope across s_in = 0/4/9 and the PRP are out-of-sample (-5); the 5-regime Pearson r (0.9998) is inflated by the WT no-defect sentinel 31.0 (L735 excludes it only from the RMSE; the perturbed-only r is 0.9986) (-2); the N_w measurement's reference is the model's own analytic law and the mib1-null reference is the 1/sqrt(12) random-phase floor (L939, L949) - internal consistency, not biology (-3); the specimen spacing reference 48.47 px is the script's own previous measurement (L958) (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py L161–L163: D_phi and sigma_omega calibrated to the ALD data (declared); tau_wash L174 chosen to land the PRP <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py#L161-L163>",
        "2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py L939–L949: N_w reference = sim_wt['n_waves_analytic'] and mib1-null reference = 0.29 random-phase floor: model-internal references <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py#L939-L949>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-measurement-delayed-kuramoto-collective-synchronization-period-t-sync-vs-autonomous-t-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-measurement-effective-in-phase-linear-stability-stiffness-kappa-eff-kappa-cos-omega-tau-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-measurement-emergent-dapt-pulse-chase-anterior-limit-of-defects-ald-at-s-in-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-measurement-emergent-dapt-washout-posterior-rescue-point-prp-for-pulse-s-in-0-s-out-9>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-measurement-kinematic-phase-waves-across-the-psm-n-w-simulated-vs-morelli-2009-analytic>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-measurement-mib1-ubiquitination-gate-late-front-coherence-r-in-mib1-null-m-0-vs-wild-type>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-measurement-riedel-kruse-2007-5-regime-emergent-ald-prp-vs-observed-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-measurement-vertebrate-embryo-sem-specimen-bilateral-somite-spacing-s-obs>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007) & Morelli et al. (2009) zebrafish Delta-Notch delayed Kuramoto phase synchrony on an advected FGF8/Wnt-graded PSM lattice: kinematic waves, Mib1-gated coupling, emergent DAPT ALD/PRP — MorphoEval overall 86.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 remediated evaluation of `2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py` (86.5/100, down from 91.3 in Pass 2). Both v2 remediation items are closed in reduced, declared form: the lattice is now an advected 24 x 12 AP x lateral delayed Kuramoto PSM under a tailbud-anchored FGF8/Wnt frequency profile with per-column period-scaled delays, producing posterior -> anterior kinematic phase waves (N_w = 1.58 vs the Law-4 analytic 1.61, anterior wavelength 2.21 S vs 2.00 S, monotone in f_A, absent for a uniform profile) that fade and recover across the DAPT pulse; and the Delta-Notch coupling is a dynamical variable kappa(t) = kappa_max u(t) g(t) with Mib1 ubiquitination kinetics and DAPT clearance (mib1-null desynchronises like early DAPT, dose sweep monotone, Mib1 restoration rescues with tau_u = 10 min). The remediation also exposed and removed Pass 2's hard-coded ALD/PRP (its 5-regime \"validation\" compared the reference JSON with itself) and an uncited instantaneous mean-field torque; ALD/PRP are now emergent (5-seed RMSE 0.22 somites, r = 0.9998) and the DAPT period lengthening is emergent in the somite count. Six Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys) back laws 1-6. The score falls because the specimen is a chick embryo mislabelled as zebrafish in Passes 1-2 and is still compared only via a fitted sinusoid, two new measurement references are model-internal, and three rate constants are calibrated to the validation data. Overall 86.5/100 (faithfulness 84.4, reproducibility 91.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/delta_notch_phase_synchrony_comparison.png: rendered output of 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py at d58a084, image/png, 1996337 B, 2436×2044 px, artifact_sha256 24bdb2e7c7c300913001ecb821a0c2953e925858f4f6af09969f9ddf45047588 (sha256 24bdb2e7c7c300913001ecb821a0c2953e925858f4f6af09969f9ddf45047588), spec_fingerprint 09e5aac12df2ce2cf18eea96b6a21a56461679db4c6b4516072331c47fa27633. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 09e5aac12df2ce2cf18eea96b6a21a56461679db4c6b4516072331c47fa27633; artifact_sha256: 24bdb2e7c7c300913001ecb821a0c2953e925858f4f6af09969f9ddf45047588; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/delta_notch_phase_synchrony/delta_notch_phase_synchrony_reference.json=209a056625b68a89..., datasets/delta_notch_phase_synchrony/scout_manifest.json=e3250a43b4bc0c22..., datasets/delta_notch_phase_synchrony/zebrafish_psm_synchrony_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007) Science 317:1911-1915 & Morelli et al. (2009) HFSP J. 3:55-66 delayed Kuramoto phase-oscillator model dtheta_i/dt = omega_i + (kappa/z)*sum_j sin(theta_j(t - tau_c) - theta_i(t)) + xi_i(t), collective frequency shift Omega = omega_0 - kappa*sin(Omega*tau_c), linear stability stiffness kappa_eff = kappa*cos(Omega*tau_c) > 0 | Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007): DAPT pulse-chase Anterior Limit of Defects ALD(s_in) = s_in + ~5.5 somites (obs 5.4 +/- 0.8, 9.6 +/- 0.9, 14.4 +/- 0.9 for s_in = 0, 4, 9) and Posterior Rescue Point PRP = 14.7 +/- 1.1 after washout at s_out = 9; mib/aei/des/bea mutants desynchronise like early DAPT | Morelli et al. (2009) frequency profile omega(x) and kinematic phase waves k = (Omega - omega(x))/v travelling posterior -> anterior; Soroldoni et al. (2014) order 1-2 waves across the zebrafish PSM, waves slowing anteriorly; Herrgen et al. (2010) DAPT lengthens the segmentation period | Itoh et al. (2003): Mind bomb E3 ubiquitin ligase ubiquitinates Delta, required for Delta endocytosis and trans-activation of Notch; mib^ta52b abolishes Delta-Notch signalling; reconstructed_in_script: Transcendental collective frequency solver and 2D (tau_c, kappa) linear stability tongue (T_sync = 22.18 min, kappa_eff = 0.0623 min^-1 at tau_c = 20.5 min vs -0.0353 min^-1 at tau_c = 11.0 min) | Advected 24 x 12 AP x lateral nearest-neighbour delayed Kuramoto PSM lattice (open AP, periodic lateral, per-column period-scaled delay) under a tailbud-anchored exponential FGF8/Wnt frequency profile (f_A = 0.5): N_w = 1.58 kinematic waves (analytic 1.61), anterior wavelength 2.21 S (analytic 2.00 S), N_w monotone in f_A (2.52 -> -0.03 for f_A 0.3 -> 1.0) | Mib1-gated coupling kappa(t) = kappa_max u(t) g(t) with ubiquitination ODE (k_ub = 0.08, k_endo = 0.02 min^-1, u_ss^WT = 0.8) and gamma-secretase gate with 8-min DAPT clearance; mib1-null late R = 0.28 (ALD 5.8), Mib1 restoration at s = 9 rescues to R = 0.77 (PRP 15.3); dose sweep monotone | Emergent ALD/PRP from R_crit = 0.5 crossings of the half-period-smoothed front lateral order parameter + Delta_n_det = 2.5: 5-seed means ALD = 5.41 / 9.21 / 14.24 (obs 5.4 / 9.6 / 14.4), PRP = 14.86 (obs 14.7), RMSE 0.22 somites, Pearson r = 0.9998 (0.9986 over the 4 perturbed regimes); somite stage clock-counted at Omega(kappa(t)) so continuous DAPT lengthens the period from 22.18 to 25.00 min | Bilateral dorsal somite row DoG peak segmentation on the vendored SEM (48.47 px mean spacing, symmetry ratio 0.9606, fitted-sinusoid r = 0.563); transfer_boundary: The frequency profile is a single exponential with f_A = 0.5 and L = 6 S chosen to land in the 1-2-wave range reported for zebrafish; it is not digitised from Morelli (2009) Fig. 3 or Soroldoni (2014) kymographs, and the N_w measurement's reference value is the model's own analytic law | tau_c(x) omega(x) = const (coupling delay scales with the local period) is this script's assumption; the Eulerian-delay alternative was not simulated | k_ub, k_endo, tau_wash, DAPT dose/IC50 and Hill n are the script's reduced rate constants; D_phi = 0.003 rad^2/min, sigma_omega = 0.014 rad/min and tau_wash = 8 min were calibrated so the emergent ALD/PRP lags match the Riedel-Kruse (2007) data (as the paper fitted its desynchronisation rate) | The SEM specimen is a chick embryo (Wikimedia 'Aves Neural tube and somites in chick embryo'), used as a vertebrate somite-metamere stand-in; no zebrafish her1/deltaC in-situ wave pattern is vendored; does_not_claim: PSM shortening and the Soroldoni (2014) Doppler contribution to the segmentation period, cell division/ingression in the tailbud, 3D cell sorting, explicit Mib1 E3-ligase stoichiometry or measured Delta endocytosis rates, or a boundary profile derived from the phase pattern (chi(s) is a coherence-gated synthetic rendering)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py:146-153, 197-200 — the reference JSON (which holds the observed regime table) is hashed but not pinned in EXPECTED_SHA256; pin it and update the digest whenever the table changes, with the change recorded in the README.",
        "remediation needed: 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py:161-162, 174 and 661-744 — D_phi, sigma_omega and tau_wash are calibrated to the ALD/PRP data the model is validated against. Hold out the PRP and the s_in = 4, 9 regimes from calibration explicitly (fit only on s_in = 0), report in-sample vs out-of-sample errors, and add seed-to-seed sd and n_lat / R_crit / Delta_n_det sensitivity to the validation table.",
        "remediation needed: 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py:172-176 — Mib1 (k_ub, k_endo) and DAPT (dose/IC50, Hill n, tau_wash) rate constants are unmeasured. Anchor k_endo to a measured Delta endocytosis/turnover half-life and the DAPT gate to a published DAPT IC50 / titration curve, or relabel the mechanism as phenomenological in the measurement names.",
        "remediation needed: 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py:284-319 and 939 — the FGF8/Wnt profile is a single exponential with f_A = 0.5 and the N_w measurement is referenced to the model's own analytic law. Vendor a digitised frequency/wave profile (Morelli 2009 Fig. 3 or Soroldoni 2014 kymograph: wave number vs PSM position, anterior wave speed) and reference N_w and the anterior wavelength ratio to it.",
        "remediation needed: 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py:413 and Panel B (L1047) — the period-scaled delay tau_c(x) omega(x) = const is asserted, not tested. Add an --eulerian-delay mode (fixed tau_c, history not advected) and report the anterior coherence loss it predicts, so the assumption is tested rather than declared.",
        "remediation needed: 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py:523-531 — advection is a discrete one-column shift with a fixed PSM length of 6 S and tailbud seeding by copying the last column; model PSM shortening (Soroldoni 2014) so the Doppler contribution to the segmentation period can be computed and compared with the reported period shift.",
        "remediation needed: 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py:590-604 and 1254-1255 — the somite boundary ribbon chi(s) is a synthetic sin^2 / salt-and-pepper rendering gated by coherence. Derive boundaries from the phase field at the front (e.g. the posterior edge of the cells whose phase crosses 0 at the determination stage) so the defective-window morphology is emergent like the ALD/PRP.",
        "remediation needed: datasets/delta_notch_phase_synchrony/zebrafish_psm_synchrony_specimen.jpg (JSON L48, README L60) and 2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py:838-847 — the only specimen is a chick SEM compared through a fitted sinusoid. Vendor a CC-licensed Danio rerio her1/deltaC in-situ or Her1-YFP live image with visible PSM stripes and compare the simulated kymograph wavelength and stripe count against it." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.65e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007) & Morelli et al. (2009) zebrafish Delta-Notch delayed Kuramoto phase synchrony on an advected FGF8/Wnt-graded PSM lattice: kinematic waves, Mib1-gated coupling, emergent DAPT ALD/PRP — Parameter expressivity: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Every new mechanism carries a sweep that behaves as claimed: the FGF8/Wnt steepness f_A controls the number of kinematic waves monotonically (N_w 2.52 -> 2.00 -> 1.58 -> 1.20 -> 0.85 -> 0.55 -> 0.26 -> -0.03 for f_A 0.3 ... 1.0, each within 0.1 of the analytic law; `sweep_frequency_profile` L747-761, Panel H inset, asserted monotone in the self-test L1319-1322); Mib1 activity M controls u_ss and the late front coherence monotonically (R 0.28 -> 0.35 -> 0.50 -> 0.81 -> ... -> 0.93 for M 0 ... 1.5, threshold crossing near M = 0.1; `sweep_mib1_dose` L764-780, Panel I inset); the DAPT onset s_in shifts the emergent ALD with unit slope (Panel D); the (tau_c, kappa) stability tongue and T_sync(tau_c) branches are kept (Panels B-C); CLI exposes --f-anterior, --mib1-dose, --tau-wash, --no-gradient, --s-in/--s-out, --seed and a --summary JSON dump (L1393-1404). Deductions: the sweeps are reported as curves, not as rendered kymographs along the sweep (-4); L, cells_per_somite, n_lat, Delta_n_det and R_crit are constants with no sweep or sensitivity (L164-168) (-4)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py L164–L168: L = 24/4 somite lengths, 12 lateral cells, R_crit and Delta_n_det are fixed constants with no sensitivity analysis <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py#L164-L168>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

