<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Riedel-Kruse et al. (2007) & Morelli et al. (2009) zebrafish Delta-Notch delayed Kuramoto phase synchrony on an advected FGF8/Wnt-graded PSM lattice: kinematic waves, Mib1-gated coupling, emergent DAPT ALD/PRP — Morphological realism / specimen match: 74/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Judged on the PNG and GIF: Panel G is a convincing kymograph of posterior -> anterior phase waves that lose lateral coherence under DAPT and recover after washout, the Panel G zoom shows the crest tilt, and the GIF ribbon shows the same waves next to the emergent defective somite window. Deductions: the vendored SEM specimen (Panel E) is a CHICK embryo per its Wikimedia title, used in Passes 1-2 as \"zebrafish_psm_synchrony_specimen\" and scored 87 for specimen match — the species label is now corrected in the JSON (L48) and README (L60) but the file remains the only biological image, so the model's organism is not matched by any specimen of that organism (-12); no her1/deltaC in-situ or live-reporter wave pattern is vendored, so the kinematic waves (the new Pass 3 output) are compared with nothing biological (-8); Panel F compares the SEM band-pass profile with a fitted sinusoid (r = 0.563, L838-847), which is a periodicity fit, not a model prediction (-4); the somite boundary ribbon chi(s) is a sin^2 + salt-and-pepper rendering gated by coherence (L590-604), not a boundary derived from the phase field (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py L590–L604: chi(s) somite boundary ribbon is a coherence-gated synthetic sin^2 / salt-and-pepper rendering <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py#L590-L604>",
        "2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py L838–L847: Panel F / segment_zebrafish_psm_specimen: fitted sinusoid at the empirical spacing vs band-pass profile (r = 0.563) - periodicity fit, not a model-to-specimen comparison <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2006-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony.py#L838-L847>",
        "datasets/delta_notch_phase_synchrony/delta_notch_phase_synchrony_reference.json L48–L48: Species field corrected to Gallus gallus (chick) per the Wikimedia source title; the specimen is not Danio rerio <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/datasets/delta_notch_phase_synchrony/delta_notch_phase_synchrony_reference.json#L48-L48>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-riedel-delta-notch-phase-synchrony-specimen-match-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.4e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

